WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.068
In the round.

2
00:00:01.228 --> 00:00:02.668
A painting is flat.

3
00:00:02.828 --> 00:00:04.407
You look at it from the front.

4
00:00:04.567 --> 00:00:06.749
A sculpture has a front, a back and sides.

5
00:00:06.909 --> 00:00:08.721
You can walk all the way round it.

6
00:00:08.881 --> 00:00:12.085
A clay pot, a statue, even a snowman is a sculpture.

7
00:00:12.785 --> 00:00:14.085
Score and slip.

8
00:00:14.245 --> 00:00:17.775
Two pieces of clay pressed together can fall apart when they dry.

9
00:00:17.935 --> 00:00:20.814
So potters score them: they scratch both pieces.

10
00:00:20.974 --> 00:00:23.157
Then they add slip, which is runny clay.

11
00:00:23.317 --> 00:00:25.778
Press, smooth, and the join lasts.

12
00:00:26.478 --> 00:00:27.871
Why won't it join?.

13
00:00:28.031 --> 00:00:30.353
When two things will not join, ask why.

14
00:00:30.513 --> 00:00:32.649
Dry clay has no water to join with.

15
00:00:32.809 --> 00:00:34.899
Smooth pebbles have nothing to grip.

16
00:00:35.059 --> 00:00:37.381
Find the reason, and you will find the fix.

17
00:00:38.081 --> 00:00:39.567
Clay from long ago.

18
00:00:39.727 --> 00:00:46.368
More than two thousand years ago, in what is now Nigeria, artists of the Nok culture made heads from clay.

19
00:00:46.528 --> 00:00:50.058
They cut the eyes, pressed in the hair, and fired the clay hard.

20
00:00:50.218 --> 00:00:51.750
Some are still here today.
